  "dom_id": "question-106809",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $N$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a|x|,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. For any $f(x)\\in N,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\nII. For any $f(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n\nIII. For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
